# Embeddable in an <iframe> on thederf.com.
#
# thederf.com serves its pages with Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy:
# credentialless (the uapp editor needs SharedArrayBuffer, hence cross-origin
# isolation). A frame inside such a page has to clear TWO checks, and this app
# is on another origin, so it needs both headers:
#
#   COEP - inherited by nested documents: a frame whose response carries no
#          COEP of its own is blocked. (Not origin-scoped: same-origin frames
#          on thederf.com need it too.)
#   CORP - COEP defaults Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy to same-origin, so a
#          CROSS-origin frame is then blocked as
#          "CorpNotSameOriginAfterDefaultedToSameOriginByCoep" even with COEP
#          set. Same-origin apps under thederf.com/ do not need this line.
#
# The alternative — the <iframe credentialless> attribute on thederf.com's
# side — also loads the page and needs neither header, but gives it a fresh
# ephemeral storage partition with no cookies, so this app would come up with
# none of the user's data.
#
# CORP: cross-origin lets any site embed this as a resource. That is already
# true today (no X-Frame-Options and no CSP frame-ancestors are set), so this
# is not a change in exposure — but adding
# `Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self' https://thederf.com`
# is how it would be locked down to thederf.com only.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: credentialless
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin
